---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="AudioLocal | Private audio converter in your browser"
  description="AudioLocal is a free audio converter that runs 100% locally. Convert MP3, WAV, OGG, AAC and FLAC in your browser without uploading files."
  path="/en/about.html"
  alternate="/about.html"
  lang="en"
  active="about"
  ogTitle="About AudioLocal"
  ogDescription="The audio converter that puts your privacy first and runs entirely in your browser."
  ogImageAlt="AudioLocal, a local and private audio converter"
>
  <article class="doc prose">
    <h1 class="title">About AudioLocal</h1>
    <p class="lead">The audio converter that respects your privacy. 100% local processing • No sign-up • Free forever.</p>

    <section class="doc-section">
      <h2>Our mission</h2>
      <p>AudioLocal was created to offer a <strong>truly private and safe</strong> alternative to traditional audio converters. Most online tools upload your files to external servers. We chose a different path: <strong>all processing happens in your own browser</strong>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section">
      <h2>What we do</h2>
      <p>AudioLocal is a web tool for converting audio files, one at a time or in batches, between the most common formats: <strong>MP3, WAV, OGG, AAC, M4A and FLAC → WAV, MP3 (128, 256, 320 kbps), OGG or AAC</strong>, depending on what your browser supports.</p>
      <h3>Privacy first</h3>
      <p>Your audio never leaves your device. We don't store it, analyze it or share it.</p>
      <h3>Fast and efficient</h3>
      <p>Conversion runs locally with your browser's Web Audio API, so there is no upload to wait for.</p>
      <h3>Full control</h3>
      <p>Choose the output format, channels (mono or stereo) and sample rate to suit your needs.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section">
      <h2>Why choose AudioLocal</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Nothing to install</li>
        <li>Works on any device (PC, Mac, Android, iOS), even offline after your first visit</li>
        <li>Completely free, with no limit on conversions (up to 150 MB and 20 minutes per file)</li>
        <li>No sign-up or account</li>
        <li>Transparent code that respects your privacy</li>
        <li>A good fit for music producers, podcasters, streamers and anyone who cares about privacy</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section">
      <h2>Our commitment</h2>
      <p>We believe your files belong to you. That's why we built a tool that doesn't depend on external servers, doesn't collect your data and leaves you in control. Our goal is to keep improving AudioLocal into the best free, private option available.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Have a question or a suggestion, or did you find a bug?<br />Write to us at: <a href="mailto:audiolocal.app@gmail.com">audiolocal.app@gmail.com</a></p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
